evidence.text:
Taking a deep, steady breath, he steps forward...

... and gives himself fully to the Maw. 

{SCRIPT: Siowan despawns. Maw opens.}

"Jherem got here through the House of Empty Time. He comes from Sagus, like us, only... centuries in the past. That's why his speech is different, why he remembers places that aren't here anymore."

She jabs your chest with a calloused finger. "Keep. This. To. Yourself. We'll tell him ourselves when we find a kind way of letting a child know that everyone he knows and loves is long dead and dust."

{JOURNAL: Journal entry here, mentioning that Jherem is from the past, and the parents don't want you to tell him. Shouldn't mention what the player is GOING to do, since there are several options.}

"Creft. Skist. In other words, precisely nothing." He holds a finger up. "That's not precisely true. I found this worthless piece of junk in a tomb, doubtless dropped there by some *other* sap duped into Tantalum's errand. Worthless. Can't even break it down for shins."

He tosses it to you. "Here. A reminder not to listen to buffoons."

{LOOT: Give Gold Merecaster}

Working with great care, you fit the delicate components together with quiet *snicks* and *clacks*, following a tentative blueprint in your mind. Unfortunately, you overestimate the strength of a crucial component, and it snaps between your fingers.

You sigh. Someone in the Order should still be able to make the device you need, but this one - though it still may be used to steal life - will be useless for Finzin and the levy's purposes.

{LOOT: "A cool, life-draining cypher" (that doesn't work for the Tormented Levy quest).}

"Haven't seen this is a while," she says softly, coming up beside you. "That's no simple circle. That's the symbol of the Children of the Endless Gate."

She snorts. "They're a sect of the Dendra O'Hur that kills people instead of eating them. They call it 'opening the cages'. The Dendra chased them out of the city a long time ago, but it doesn't look like they took the hint. Either that or..." She pauses, thinking. "One of the Dendra O'Hur got tired of waiting for people to die on their own."
{MATKINA}

Indigo waves rise in the wake of the huge marteling whale bearing down on Sagus Cliffs. Its flank blocks out the sun; its shadow sweeps over your meager dhow and a whole swath of sea.

From high up on the beast's back, a lookout leans down. "Plague!" he cries, in a voice that seems too faint, even considering the distance. His warning is unnecessary: the yellowjack flag flapping from the mast can be seen all the way from the city.

As the lookout stares directly at your dhow, he cocks his head quizzically and rubs his eyes, plainly confused to see no one in the boat. The light-bender on your belt does its work well... while its charge lasts.

After a moment, the man wanders off.

{ART: The Whale.}
{[A] SOUND: Waves lapping against the dhow.}

"You... you... you!" He sputters, and then realizes that he's getting dangerously close to you. He yelps, grabs a handful of his junk, and disappears from the room. You're not quite sure how he left.

He didn't take everything, though. You find an oddly shaped item amongst what's left.

{LOOT: Drop Silver Merecaster.}

"Praise the Devourer!" He embraces you, eyes wild and feverish. The other cultists caper about, bending and twisting in exultation.

Releasing you suddenly, he rummages in a pocket and drops a handful of shins into your hand, along with a small device. "Payment from the Extremities, in the manner of the outside world. But the greater reward is the favor you have earned from our god."

{LOOT}

"Bloom-flesh, my friend. Bloom-flesh! We craft everything out of it - clothing, armor, building materials, jerky, you name it! The Bloom cultists in particular love wrapping themselves in Bloom-flesh, but everybody buys from us - even the murdens!"

"You might say our business is... blooming!" He raises his eyebrows at you expectantly.

{WORDPLAY}

[Your struggles drive the creature off but also manage to shake loose something of value. You quickly reach the surface, your unexpected prize in tow.]

{SCRIPT:  Give the player something cool. Maybe a Bloom Pearl of some sort?}

{LOOT}

She's expecting a battle of words, and when you strike her on the chin, she spins once and then sits heavily. She stares dazedly at you for a moment, and scrambles backward before staggering to her feet. 

She touches a stud on the table, and it folds into a small box. Keeping a wary eye on you, she reaches out and takes its handle, and then turns and bolts.

Looking down, you notice that she dropped one of her injectors in her haste to get away.

{SCRIPT:  Need to make her run away and despawn.}

{SCRIPT:  Need to give out an injector cypher.}

{LOOT - Laarna's Injector}

She's expecting a battle of words, and when you strike her on the chin, she spins once and then sits heavily. She stares dazedly at you for a moment, and scrambles backward before staggering to her feet. 

She touches a stud on the table, and it folds into a small box. Keeping a wary eye on you, she reaches out and takes its handle, and then turns and bolts.

Looking down, you notice that she dropped one of her injectors and a dirty knife in her haste to get away.

{SCRIPT:  Need to make her run away and despawn.}

{SCRIPT:  Need to hand out an injector cypher, maybe a knife that applies the diseased fettle when it strikes an enemy}

{LOOT - ESSENTIAL - Laarna's Injector}

She stares at you, her mouth slightly open, and she remains that way for a good minute. She snaps back to reality and looks down at her hands. Disgust dawns over her features as she considers what she is doing, and she throws down her tools.

She turns and vomits.

"Oh, no. No, no no. The Bloom whispered to me, and I listened. What have I done?" She rushes away, leaving her tools behind.

The ground rumbles under your feet, and you feel a wave of malice from the Bloom-flesh.

{SCRIPT:  Need to remove her from the scene in some way.}

{SCRIPT:  Need to hand out an injector cypher, maybe a knife that applies the diseased fettle when it strikes an enemy}

{LOOT - ESSENTIAL - Laarna's Injector}

"A psychic attack is slowly destroying my body. Can you help?"
{SCRIPT: Node 120 should only be visible so long as the PC has the Specter's Decay fettle. After it's cured, Node 120, 121, and 122 should be hidden.}
{SCRIPT: Please note that the Specter fettle may not be in game anymore.}

"A psychic attack is slowly destroying my body. Will you help me?"
{SCRIPT: Node 142 should only be visible so long as the PC has the Specter's Decay fettle.}
{SCRIPT: Please note that the Specter fettle may not be in game anymore.}

Digging your fingers deep under the scale, you rip and tug with all your strength. At last, the scale snaps off, revealing a tube-like fistula leading into the megalith's interior.

As a small object rolls out of the tube, your mind explodes with the megalith's outrage. <No no. Bad hatchling. No bubbles.> Then, its thoughts fall silent.

{LOOT: An item inferior to the Zero Sum Engine.}

{HUB 1.0 Cave Approach}
{TimeEnglish = LATE NIGHT}
Late night cloaks the cave approach in darkness. Far below, the village lights twinkle.

You hear shouts of alarm from the enclosure near the monolith, and the ground shakes from the thudding steps of the war-mantis. You order the others to take cover and they hit the mud just as the construct tops the low ridge, haloed by the light behind it and dripping with rain. 

It pauses on the ridge top, examining the dead patrols, then starts limping forward, its head swiveling back and forth, looking for movement. It's only a matter of time before it finds you all. Staying still is not an option. You must make a move.

{SOUND: Robot Movement.}
{ART: Illustration - The Construct Scanning}

Vostiel turns the launcher and calculates distance and trajectory, then loads a spherical cypher and squeezes the firing bulb. With a sound like a popping cork, the plasma detonator flies toward the shoulder of the dead construct and hits dead on. One moment the crew is crouched down, firing the heater, the next, they are enveloped in a swirling orange conflagration and their limbs are flying everywhere. 

A moment later the heater explodes too, caving in the massive head of the old construct and causing it to slump forward as if it was falling asleep. 

{SOUND: Fiery explosion.}
{ART: Illustration - Blowing up the Heater}

As one, you and Vostiel lob your detonators. Vostiel's bounces right into the enclosure, and you hear the troopers' shriek in fear as they try to escape it. With its inhuman reaction time, however, the construct catches yours in its remaining pincer, but it's not fast enough to stop it from detonating. 

Unfortunately, it *is* fast enough to get off one more shot before the cypher's implosion collapses it and everything around it into a single point. A searing beam stabs through you from clavicle to pelvis, cooking everything in between. 

"Captain!" shouts Vostiel. He turns you over. "Moon of Fortune, you're alive! You got it, captain! The big bastard is dead! And the squad too!"

{SOUND: Two sonic booms.}
{ART: Illustration - Blowing up the Construct}

