evidence.text:
"If you are truly the ruler of the Bloom, then you should also be the mistress of your own life. Control your destiny, and choose... rather than letting others act upon you. This is the truth of power."

{SCRIPT:  Can collase this and the two nodes below into a single one once assets are confirmed working.}

{CRIT}

after.translation:
她看起来也像是正要咽下什么恶心的东西。“我感激你。”

她快步走向出口，她的打手紧随其后。

{SCRIPT: Fire a cutscene wherein the Memovira abandons her fortress with her followers (i.e., they exit and despawn).}

evidence.text:
She also looks like she's about to swallow something disgusting. "You have my gratitude."

She walks quickly to the exit, her thugs close at her heels.

{SCRIPT: Fire a cutscene wherein the Memovira abandons her fortress with her followers (i.e., they exit and despawn).}

Then, the voices are gone and your senses return to you: the scrape of your foot on stone, the sound of your heartbeat in your ears.

You're back where you were before you entered the Endless Gate. The Gate is gone. And so is Inifere.

{NOTE: Ends the conversation, ends the Crisis, Inifere leaves the VoDH, TEH quest is completed, TSC quest is failed if active. Move party back to Marcysa's tomb / entry to The Endless Gate.  Gate is now closed, Inifere is now gone.}

He looks at you, seeing you for the first time, then at the shin in your hand. His eyes light up. "Ha! I knew you'd come back for me. And you smuggled a shaper key past those damn gibbers."

He takes the shin from your hand. Then he kneels down and works at some device you can't see. There is an audible click, the ghibra around you swim away, and the haunted look drops from Mazzof's natural eye.

{SOUND: Click, like a heavy lock being successfully picked.}

As you stumble across the street to the cool interior of the Drowned Gibber, the world swims around you and you feel yourself yanked out of the mere and back into your own body. 

{Mere ends.}

{NATHAN: You're right that this feels too abrupt. In our other Meres, this sort of choice would usually lead to a different branch or eventually to the same branch but from a different path.}

"But... but..." Her already red face turns redder as she realizes the truth of your words. Her fists clench. "It's not fair! This was the chance of a lifetime!"

As she starts sobbing into her hands and you stumble down the street toward the cool interior of the Drowned Gibber, the world swims around you and you feel yourself yanked out of the mere and back into your own body. 

{Mere ends.}

By the time we'd reached the Enstal line we'd had enough. The whole squad was in agreement, Hyrnhol had to go. He'd already got half of us killed in the Dool thanks to his cowardice and shilly-shallying, and his decision at Bresadt proved he hadn't gained any wisdom since. The only question was how to do it. Outright murder would get us all the chop, and the higher-ups were wise to the usual friendly-fire and "accidental" ordinance malfunction ploys. We had to be subtle.  

Then Gerrisae hit on it. We'd all heard Hyrnhal moaning about his wife leaving him, and so had the brass. If we wrote a note in his hand saying her betrayal had driven him to the brink, well, who'd gainsay it?

{SCRIPT: Is it possible to set the text of the book in italic, or differentiate it from the normal discriptive text of the Mere?}
