"Sure. They have lots of names. 'Raven-men', for one. Cal..." he grimaces at the recollection, but forges on regardless. "Callistege called them 'dulsein' for some reason."

He lowers his voice. "Point is, don't give them an excuse to attack. That includes threatening them... or not threatening them enough."
{ALIGERN}

You quickly explain what the Healer has given you, and hand the inoculation to the Whalesinger. He presses the needle through his skin, blending the serum with his blood.

There is no change or wonderment worked by the injection: no esotery lies behind this treatment, merely a child's life. All the same, the Whalesinger nods and thanks you. "You have safeguarded my song, and thus the Haven."

{[B] SOUND: High-tech auto-injector sound sound, maybe more of a hiss sound than anything, like the injectors on Babylon 5.}

