There is no change or wonderment worked by the injection: no esotery lies behind this treatment, merely a child's life. All the same, the Whalesinger nods and thanks you. "You have safeguarded my song, and thus the Haven."

{[B] SOUND: High-tech auto-injector sound sound, maybe more of a hiss sound than anything, like the injectors on Babylon 5.}

Your squad spreads out and takes cover in the rubble along the path of the enemy patrols, then takes them out as they pass with silent sliver spitters tipped with arcane chemicals that paralyze them before they can sound the alarm.

All except the last one. A misfire allows the final scout a squawk of surprise before he dies.

{SOUND: Energy weapon fire.}

You flip open the cover of the Tome of Singing Thorns. On the title page is a castoff's tattoo divided into five curving, triangular shapes the color of each Tide, with a small inscription beneath. You try turning to the next page, but can't - it's as if the pages are a solid block of paper. 

You lay your hand on the title page's rough, somewhat metallic surface, and the sharp triangular shapes spring up around your fingers with a vibrating hum. 

{SOUND: Each thorn mentioned in this conversation plays a unique note. The puzzle is solved by playing them in ascending order. This melody was a lullaby sung by TCG to his daughter before he became the utter jerkwad we know. Each time the player plays a right note, it sustains, joining the others. When they screw up, the notes fade out, and the player starts over. Let me know if you have any questions, or if you don't have the time to come up with a song. I can throw something together if that's the case.}

"It's quite safe," he says, nodding. "Most of the time. In almost three out of five cases. And the procedure couldn't be simpler. The drones simply saw your skull open, shove an implant into the right spot and seal everything back up again."

He clasps his hands. "Once they do that, the implant will help you identify the purposes of unknown numenera. It costs [Global: a2201_JernaughNumeneraAnalyzerPrice] shins, but it pays for itself!" 

{MONEY}

"Ah, poor Manth. He was always up for anything, but just never had that 'hairs on the back of your neck' sense that you need on the street. Not a born reader of signs, if you get me."

"You can bet I wouldn't have been caught unawares by... whatever it was that done for him. At least I hope not."
{COLIN/NATHAN: This also feels like it should maybe be a forced interjection, or if it's otherwise, then it should be reworded to assume the player might hear about it long after the event in question. -AH}

